                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2f46ce62-e27b-3e44-9170-90d740803ea9",
                        "entry_id": "bd46d8e4-7cd5-31f4-93b7-8942ec674fb8",
                        "glosses": [
                            "to smear oneself"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f44160cc-f4de-4895-85c9-e2925c27a566",
                                "sense_id": "2f46ce62-e27b-3e44-9170-90d740803ea9",
                                "text": "Она́ уже́ не по́мнила ни лу́нного ве́чера на Во́лге, ни объясне́ний в любви́, ни поэти́ческой жи́зни в избе́, а по́мнила то́лько, что она́ из пусто́й при́хоти, из баловства́, вся, с рука́ми и с нога́ми, вы́мазалась во что́-то гря́зное, ли́пкое, от чего́ никогда́ уж не отмо́ешься...",
                                "translation": "She no longer thought of the moon-light Volga night, the love avowal, the romance of life in the peasant's hut; she remembered only that from caprice and selfishness she had smeared herself from head to feet with something vile and sticky which no washing would wash away.",
                                "english": "She no longer thought of the moon-light Volga night, the love avowal, the romance of life in the peasant's hut; she remembered only that from caprice and selfishness she had smeared herself from head to feet with something vile and sticky which no washing would wash away."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
